
[TestSuperFirstStatement/invalid-0 - 1]
Diagnostic 1: superNotFirst (10:5 - 10:21)
Message: 'super()' must be the first statement of the constructor: until it has run 'this' does not exist, so anything above it cannot reach the base class's state.
Help: Move 'super()' to the top of the constructor.
   9 |     const value = work();
  10 |     super({ value });
     |     ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  11 |   }
